Q: React displays old text when a opacity animation is applied A: <p>This fixes the behavior of the text from one state being overlayed on the text of the previous state, but it still makes no sense to me. Will chalk it up to the joys of front end development. If anyone can explain it let me know.</p>
<p>This change to the CSS fixes the behavior:</p>
<pre><code>@keyframes throb {
    0% {
        opacity: 0.3;
    }

    50% {
        opacity: 1;
    }

    100% {
        opacity: 0.3;
    }
}
</code></pre>
